#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186171786 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d15f8fa8-f265-50da-b172-3ccb90895448" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Connected Regions"}] :question/id #uuid "8cbffe56-0a93-59c5-9ea8-c4040e07bb03" :question/math-academy-id "e-8682" :question/problem "Which of the following regions are connected?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3357/Source/Images/8bc6eee716b3c35ded2c54628da21226.png)" :question/worked-solution "A region $D$ is connected if every pair of points in $D$ can be joined by a smooth curve or a path in $D$.\n\nAmong the given options, only regions I, II, and III satisfy this definition.\n\nRegion IV does not satisfy this definition. Note that if we take two points $P$ and $Q$, as shown below, there is no path lying entirely within the region that connects them.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3357/Source/Images/4c9ec6c4f35d8902525483f7a86d70af.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186171787 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d1af47ea-6253-5d58-9b94-31e52de27106" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Simply-Connected Regions"}] :question/id #uuid "053b6396-341c-5b1f-a942-ca1fbf6efa7a" :question/math-academy-id "e-8684" :question/problem "Which of the regions shown below are simply connected?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3357/Source/Images/1164dfedfd68fecee2af1031295ffb86.png)" :question/worked-solution "A connected region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ can be contracted to a point.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3357/Source/Images/06bab6e6cec4b75e4a1363b4dbc20310.png)\n\nA connected *plane* region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ encloses only points in $D$. In other words, the region does not contain any holes. Plane regions containing holes are not simply connected, since some simple closed curves cannot be contracted to a point:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3357/Source/Images/42d126c7bd2ac311262b659d2596dc37.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the regions:\n\n- Region I is not simply connected. Instead, this is a connected region that contains a hole.\n- Region II is simply connected. This is a connected region that does not contain holes.\n- Region III is not simply connected. Instead, this is a region that consists of two pieces (it's not connected).\n- Region IV is simply connected. This is a connected region that does not contain holes.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and IV only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186171829 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "280e7ba4-7617-546b-9e0d-a5bdc33dad8d" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Simply-Connected Regions in Euclidian Space"}] :question/id #uuid "fb87998f-3236-510b-94aa-7db80487d8c9" :question/math-academy-id "e-9498" :question/problem "Which of the following regions are simply connected?\n\n1. $\\{(x,y) \\in \\mathbb R^2 \\: \\mid \\: y-x\\geq 0\\}$\n2. $\\{(x,y) \\in \\mathbb R^2 \\: \\mid \\: (x,y)\\neq (0,0)\\}$\n3. $\\{(x,y)\\in \\mathbb R^2 \\: \\mid \\: x^2+y^2> 4\\}$" :question/worked-solution "A connected region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ can be contracted to a point.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3357/Source/Images/998c3fae4e98a4fcb65db22d9a3b178a.png)\n\nA connected *plane* region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ encloses only points in $D$. In other words, the region does not contain any holes. Plane regions containing holes are not simply connected, since some simple closed curves cannot be contracted to a point:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3357/Source/Images/06500334cbe214f995d2491dc71265a1.png)\n\nLet's now examine our regions in turn.\n\n- Region I is simply connected. Indeed, it is the half-plane $y \\geq x$. So, it's a plane region without holes.\n- Region II is *not* simply connected since it's a plane region with a hole at $(0,0)$.\n- Region III is *not* simply connected since it's a plane region with a hole. In this case, the hole contains all points on the disc $x^2+y^2 \\leq 4$.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172592 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d15f8fa8-f265-50da-b172-3ccb90895448" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Connected Regions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f09971ee-e0b1-5368-b43f-c0ddce3cf5c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3357/Source/Images/q-98032-a-3.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186171518} {:answer/id #uuid "f3fdf4cf-d194-5a0e-bf0f-f714f390c8e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3357/Source/Images/q-98032-a-5.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186171519} {:answer/id #uuid "2a83c0a3-26bc-5b40-851b-313168b9c6ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3357/Source/Images/q-98032-a-1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186171520} {:answer/id #uuid "5b1e9073-fa5f-5949-a5f2-ec63cafa0632" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3357/Source/Images/q-98032-a-4.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186171521} {:answer/id #uuid "7b7bd01c-ef6b-58e9-a50a-b357226fb10a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3357/Source/Images/q-98032-a-2.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186171522}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2a83c0a3-26bc-5b40-851b-313168b9c6ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3357/Source/Images/q-98032-a-1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186171520} :answer-field/id #uuid "9dba4603-85b6-5c93-905c-c5a0334b6448" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186171517}] :question/id 